**1. A flexible lighting element comprising:**

a flexible substrate having a front side and a rear side;

a plurality of conductive elements disposed on the front side of the flexible substrate;

at least one light emitter having an emission surface and first and second electrical contacts located on a rear surface opposite the emission surface, the first and second electrical contacts being electrically coupled to respective ones of the plurality of conductive elements;

an optically transparent adhesive layer overlying and securing the at least one light emitter and at least a portion of the plurality of conductive elements to the flexible substrate; and

an optically transparent protective layer overlying the adhesive layer and the at least one light emitter,

wherein the emission surface is configured to emit light through the adhesive layer and the protective layer,

wherein the adhesive layer and the protective layer collectively have an average visible-light transmittance of at least 80% over a wavelength range from 400 nm to 700 nm, and

wherein, when the flexible lighting element is viewed from a viewing side defined by the protective layer under ambient illumination of 1,000 lux at a viewing distance of 30 cm, the plurality of conductive elements is not individually discernible by an unaided human eye.

1. **A flexible lighting device comprising:**

a flexible first substrate;

first and second conductive elements disposed on the first substrate;

a light-emitting component comprising first and second contacts arranged substantially coplanar with one another and a light-emitting surface opposite the first and second contacts, the first and second contacts being electrically coupled to the first and second conductive elements, respectively; and

a plurality of transparent layers overlying the light-emitting surface, the transparent layers collectively transmitting at least 70% of light emitted by the light-emitting component through the light-emitting surface.
